116270,"n":"compartment::endoplasmic reticulum","v":"1.542519","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"stringdb::description","v":"Acid-sensing ion channel 3; Cation channel with high affinity for sodium, which is gated by extracellular protons and inhibited by the diuretic amiloride. Generates a biphasic current with a fast inactivating and a slow sustained phase. In sensory neurons is proposed to mediate the pain induced by acidosis that occurs in ischemic, damaged or inflamed tissue. May be involved in hyperalgesia. May play a role in mechanoreception. Heteromeric channel assembly seems to modulate channel properties."},{"po":116270,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"1.156256","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"display name","v":"ASIC3"},{"po":116270,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"1.543548","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"0.181818","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"1.263316454382707","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":116270,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.04498","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(117,239,235)"},{"po":116270,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000297512"},{"po":116270,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"1.939573","d":"double"},{"po":116270,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"0.990081","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"padj","v":"0.0103361599924392","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":116267,"n":"compartment::golgi apparatus","v":"1.197191","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"0.732394","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"2.480442","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["AF-Q9ULE3"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":116267,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"0.307017","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":116267,"n":"compartment::peroxisome","v":"0.46875","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n":"tissue::liver","v":"4.222313","d":"double"},{"po":116267,"n