romeric calcium-permeable ion channel formed by PKD1 and PKD2 that is activated by interaction between PKD1 and a Wnt family member, such as WNT3A and WNT9B. Both PKD1 and PKD2 are required for channel activity. Involved in renal tubulogenesis. Involved in fluid- flow mechanosensation by the primary cilium in renal epithelium (By similarity). Acts as a regulator of cilium length, together with PKD2 (By similarity). The dynamic control of cilium length is essential in the regulation of mechanotransductive signaling (By similarity). The cilium length resp [...] "},{"po":115802,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"1.676243","d":"double"},{"po":115802,"n":"display name","v":"PKD1"},{"po":115802,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.045775","d":"double"},{"po":115802,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"1.953038","d":"double"},{"po":115802,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"0.8528822506173086","d":"double"},{"po":115802,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":115802,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.647445","d":"double"},{"po":115802,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(117,182,239)"},{"po":115802,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000262304"},{"po":115802,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"2.410434","d":"double"},{"po":115802,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"2.243587","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":115796,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"1.360467","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"1.703968","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["2ybb_V","5iy5_K","AF-P24311"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":115796,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"1.537189","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":115796,"n":"compartment::peroxisome","v":"1.041822","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"tissue::liver","v":"4.152038","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"compartment::extracellular","v":"1.246499","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"tissue::stomach","v":"1.594761","d":"double"},{"po":115796,"n":"tissue::bone marrow","v":"2.2209